WEBVTT

00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:15.478
<v><b>Ela:</b></v> To be honest, er there are quite a few things that I like, er that I prefer to do on my own.

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:21.583
For instance, when I am reading or studying or just trying to get things done, I,

00:00:21.603 --> 00:00:32.525
I value peace and quiet. Er, I find it much easier to, focus when there isn’t anyone around to,

00:00:32.871 --> 00:00:35.276
to interrupt my train of thought.

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:40.997
I sometimes, quite often actually, er, travel alone.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:45.609
I like travelling alone because I like feeling independent.

00:00:45.916 --> 00:00:52.543
Er, and also, I’m, when I travel alone, I’m more open to, er, new experiences.

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:58.747
I notice more, er, and, and also, I travel at my own pace.

00:01:05.094 --> 00:01:08.987
<v><b>Begoña:</b></v> There are things that I prefer to do alone, such as going shopping.

00:01:09.446 --> 00:01:13.822
And when I go shopping, I sometimes find it quite difficult to make up my mind.

00:01:14.069 --> 00:01:17.777
So I prefer to be alone and not to have anybody waiting for me.

00:01:18.137 --> 00:01:21.865
That way, I have time to decide what to do and what to buy.

00:01:27.778 --> 00:01:31.288
<v><b>Geoffrey:</b></v> I absolutely love watching movies all on my own.

00:01:31.742 --> 00:01:37.256
It’s the best thing in the world, lying on my sofa in the living room, watching television,

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.100
nobody around and nobody interfering, nobody talking over the actors.

00:01:41.199 --> 00:01:47.220
And I can watch the movie as I please, I can pause when I want, I can go back.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.870
I can rewind to watch some bits. And yeah, that’s the best way to enjoy a really good movie.

00:01:58.612 --> 00:02:00.345
<v><b>Ross:</b></v> I prefer to work alone.

00:02:00.465 --> 00:02:03.240
Um, I know that might sound odd, but when it comes,

00:02:03.279 --> 00:02:08.964
a lot of my work revolves around stuff like video editing, as well as teaching.

00:02:09.558 --> 00:02:13.937
And I’ve, well you’re in front of a computer, basically.

00:02:14.223 --> 00:02:19.725
Um, some people like to do that type of thing with others who kind of comment

00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:24.738
on their work as they’re doing it and give them advice, and that’s great. I, I agree with that.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.961
But I’ve always felt like I work better and faster when I’m working on my own.

00:02:29.254 --> 00:02:36.085
Um, I tend to be more imaginative and creative, and I think that’s because I’m, you know,

00:02:36.175 --> 00:02:41.173
you’re not self-conscious about what other people think when you’re working away on your own,

00:02:41.373 --> 00:02:42.733
you’re just getting on with it.